description: Prefer ASCII hyphen (-) over em/en dashes in copy and UI text
alwaysApply: true
---

# No em or en dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in user-facing copy, UI strings, comments, commit messages, or docs you write for this project.

Use a regular hyphen-minus (`-`) instead.

```text
❌ act on—before schedules slip
✅ act on - before schedules slip

❌ 1–10 employees
✅ 1-10 employees

❌ Next.js — React
✅ Next.js - React
```

When editing existing text, replace any `—` or `–` with `-`.
